WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:44.087
[ Watch on KissFlix.co ]

2
00:44.357 --> 00:48.069
‎DOCTOR X: MAFIA IN WHITE

3
01:16.264 --> 01:18.474
‎Gye Su-jeong? Are you Gye Su-jeong?

4
01:20.685 --> 01:21.561
‎Who are you?

5
01:22.061 --> 01:23.479
‎The hands of God?

6
01:23.563 --> 01:25.356
‎Doctor X?

7
01:44.584 --> 01:47.170
‎My little sister was shot.

8
01:47.253 --> 01:48.922
‎She needs you, Gye Su-jeong.

9
01:51.382 --> 01:52.634
‎Is that why you came here

10
01:54.135 --> 01:56.179
‎all by yourself?

11
01:57.513 --> 02:01.142
‎I heard only Gye Su-jeong can save her.

12
02:02.769 --> 02:04.187
‎Who told you that?

13
02:04.771 --> 02:05.605
‎Baba.

14
02:06.940 --> 02:07.899
‎Baba?

15
02:07.982 --> 02:09.776
‎He's a doctor.

16
02:09.859 --> 02:12.612
‎Baba is hurt too, and he says

17
02:12.695 --> 02:15.740
‎there's a bullet ‎in my little sister's head.

18
02:18.201 --> 02:20.620
‎Please help us.

19
02:45.061 --> 02:47.480
‎Okay. Let's go.

20
03:05.123 --> 03:06.124
‎What's this?

21
03:14.674 --> 03:16.759
‎There are a lot of soldiers outside.

22
03:16.843 --> 03:18.678
‎I'll only get in your way.

23
03:18.761 --> 03:22.056
‎-That's where my village is-- ‎-No.

24
03:23.141 --> 03:25.268
‎You need

25
03:26.102 --> 03:27.687
‎medical treatment too.

26
03:27.770 --> 03:29.397
‎Then…

27
03:31.399 --> 03:32.233
‎Why…

28
03:33.234 --> 03:34.527
‎Why?

29
03:34.610 --> 03:36.696
‎Bullets might come from behind.

30
03:37.405 --> 03:41.451
‎You must survive to save my little sister.

31
03:53.504 --> 03:56.090
‎What if the bullets

32
03:57.091 --> 03:58.092
‎come from the front?

33
04:21.407 --> 04:22.617
‎What's your name?

34
04:23.534 --> 04:24.744
‎Baraka.

35
04:26.454 --> 04:27.413
‎"Blessing"?

36
04:30.124 --> 04:31.209
‎And your little sister?

37
04:31.793 --> 04:32.668
‎Neema.

38
04:34.796 --> 04:36.130
‎"Blessing" and "Grace."

39
04:36.964 --> 04:40.218
‎With those on our side, ‎nothing bad will happen to us.

40
04:42.970 --> 04:43.971
‎Close your eyes.

41
04:52.647 --> 04:54.440
‎Don't open your eyes

42
04:55.441 --> 04:56.901
‎until I say that you can.

43
04:58.820 --> 05:02.281
‎When you open your eyes, ‎you'll see your little sister.

44
05:02.365 --> 05:03.241
‎Your little sister.

45
05:06.661 --> 05:07.495
‎So…

46
05:09.414 --> 05:10.623
‎hold on tight.

47
05:16.129 --> 05:18.423
‎Let's go home.

48
05:26.722 --> 05:29.600
‎DOCTOR X: MAFIA IN WHITE

49
05:37.775 --> 05:39.152
‎This just in.

50
05:39.235 --> 05:42.530
‎Former President Ji Du-seok ‎has been found unconscious

51
05:42.613 --> 05:44.782
‎and is being rushed to the hospital.

52
05:45.366 --> 05:48.494
‎Our reporter at the scene has more.

53
05:56.961 --> 06:00.840
‎GUSEO UNIVERSITY SEONAM MEDICAL CENTER

54
06:07.930 --> 06:09.765
‎Did you find Mr. Oh Sang-beom?

55
06:11.100 --> 06:12.185
‎Where is he?

56
06:12.852 --> 06:14.020
‎Tell me where he is!

57
06:16.022 --> 06:18.107
‎I can stay longer. Let me stay.

58
06:18.191 --> 06:20.026
‎An intern can't stay here the whole time.

59
06:20.109 --> 06:21.027
‎I'll stay instead.

60
06:21.110 --> 06:25.907
‎OH SANG-BEOM

61
06:27.825 --> 06:31.495
‎The head of hospital security came earlier

62
06:31.579 --> 06:33.915
‎and said he'll need to be moved ‎to another room.

63
06:34.415 --> 06:36.000
‎Moved to another room? Why?

64
06:36.083 --> 06:38.461
‎They need to clear this entire floor,

65
06:38.544 --> 06:40.338
‎so they'll find another room for him.

66
06:40.421 --> 06:42.215
‎They made a big show of welcoming him

67
06:42.298 --> 06:44.634
‎and put him in a VIP room ‎like they'd do anything for him.

68
06:44.717 --> 06:46.427
‎But now this?

69
06:49.722 --> 06:51.724
‎Let her stay for now.

70
06:51.807 --> 06:53.309
‎She won't budge, no matter who comes.

71
06:54.894 --> 06:56.187
‎Damn it.

72
07:08.950 --> 07:10.660
‎I'll speak to the director about this.

73
07:10.743 --> 07:12.286
‎Director Bu probably approved it already.

74
07:12.370 --> 07:14.580
‎Even if he did, ‎we still need to tell him this is wrong.

75
07:15.581 --> 07:17.833
‎The hospital agreed to take ‎full responsibility for that patient.

76
07:17.917 --> 07:20.211
‎He didn't want to come, ‎but we dragged him here.

77
07:20.795 --> 07:22.004
‎Yes, but…

78
07:22.088 --> 07:23.714
‎Staying here doesn't feel right either.

79
07:25.967 --> 07:27.176
‎Right.

80
07:27.260 --> 07:30.429
‎But still, what kind of situation is this?

81
07:30.513 --> 07:32.390
‎How does this make any sense?

82
07:39.230 --> 07:41.190
‎WE CONDEMN JI DU-SEOK, A BLIGHT ON HISTORY

83
07:41.274 --> 07:43.317
‎HOPE DAILY

84
07:46.362 --> 07:48.155
‎JI DU-SEOK, APOLOGIZE TO THE PEOPLE!

85
07:48.239 --> 07:49.490
‎BRING DOWN JI DU-SEOK

86
08:08.801 --> 08:12.013
‎A WEEK AGO

87
08:38.164 --> 08:39.415
‎-Hello, sir. ‎-Hello, sir.

88
08:42.084 --> 08:42.918
‎Hello.

89
08:51.594 --> 08:52.470
‎Working hard, I see.

90
09:04.690 --> 09:06.901
‎You could've given us a little heads-up.

91
09:06.984 --> 09:08.944
‎To what do we owe ‎the pleasure of this sudden visit?

92
09:09.028 --> 09:10.196
‎To catch you off guard.

93
09:11.238 --> 09:14.200
‎Goodness, if that was your intention, ‎you definitely succeeded.

94
09:14.283 --> 09:16.327
‎Director Bu, you also seemed surprised.

95
09:17.620 --> 09:21.457
‎I couldn't help but wonder ‎what could bring you here unannounced.

96
09:21.540 --> 09:22.875
‎Where do I even begin?

97
09:25.086 --> 09:27.213
‎We'd love to hear your thoughts.

98
09:27.797 --> 09:28.673
‎Actually,

99
09:28.756 --> 09:32.343
‎I was thinking about the suggestion ‎you made at the Magnolia gathering.

100
09:32.426 --> 09:35.262
‎You know, forming a task force ‎for hospital management recovery…

101
09:35.346 --> 09:36.305
‎Do a surgery for us.

102
09:37.556 --> 09:40.518
‎Surgery? What surgery?

103
09:42.520 --> 09:45.106
‎The patient should come in with a referral

104
09:45.189 --> 09:46.732
‎and get examined--

105
09:46.816 --> 09:50.653
‎Would Chairman Gu be here ‎if we could go through proper channels?

106
09:51.195 --> 09:52.321
‎I'm not sure what you mean.

107
09:53.114 --> 09:55.825
‎-Could you be more specific? ‎-We need you to remove a bullet.

108
10:00.788 --> 10:05.918
‎VICTIMS STILL OVERLOOKED AS SUPPORT STALLS ‎46 YEARS AFTER GWANGJU DEMOCRATIC UPRISING

109
10:11.257 --> 10:12.133
‎From here.

110
10:15.261 --> 10:16.095
‎What?

111
10:18.597 --> 10:20.349
‎VICTIMS STILL OVERLOOKED

112
10:20.433 --> 10:22.601
‎The patient is a 57-year-old male, ‎Oh Sang-beom.

113
10:22.685 --> 10:25.062
‎He suffered ‎a traumatic brain injury in 1980

114
10:25.146 --> 10:27.898
‎and fell into a coma ‎from a lodged bullet fragment,

115
10:27.982 --> 10:29.483
‎but woke up 15 days later.

116
10:30.401 --> 10:31.819
‎The injury site is right here.

117
10:31.902 --> 10:33.487
‎CASE 1: OH SANG-BEOM, M/57

118
10:33.571 --> 10:35.114
‎It was left in place

119
10:35.197 --> 10:38.117
‎because the surgical techniques ‎and tools back then

120
10:38.200 --> 10:39.618
‎made removal too risky.

121
10:41.078 --> 10:46.083
‎Because of its location, it still triggers ‎left-sided facial and limb spasms,

122
10:46.167 --> 10:50.880
‎PTSD-induced seizures, headaches, ‎and visual and auditory hallucinations.

123
10:52.923 --> 10:54.008
‎After that happened,

124
10:54.091 --> 10:57.094
‎a fire broke out at the hospital ‎and took out his records.

125
10:57.720 --> 10:59.764
‎So there's no way to know ‎its exact location.

126
10:59.847 --> 11:03.058
‎-Why not examine him again then? ‎-He said no.

127
11:03.142 --> 11:06.729
‎He's refusing treatment ‎and just taking a ton of painkillers.

128
11:06.812 --> 11:09.398
‎His older brother was with him at the time

129
11:09.482 --> 11:13.486
‎and died from the shooting ‎while shielding him.

130
11:13.569 --> 11:15.738
‎He feels guilty or whatever

131
11:15.821 --> 11:18.532
‎and insists on just living with it.

132
11:18.616 --> 11:21.452
‎Anyway, this man is important because

133
11:21.535 --> 11:22.870
‎he was shot from a helicopter.

134
11:24.121 --> 11:24.955
‎You get it, right?

135
11:25.623 --> 11:28.876
‎Mr. Oh and his brother ‎weren't shot by just any gun.

136
11:28.959 --> 11:30.794
‎They were shot from a helicopter.

137
11:30.878 --> 11:33.005
‎The martial law command ‎never really acknowledged

138
11:33.088 --> 11:35.758
‎any acts of violence ‎by their troops at the time.

139
11:35.841 --> 11:37.092
‎But proof of that

140
11:38.636 --> 11:40.095
‎is in this man's head.

141
11:40.763 --> 11:43.849
‎But you said he refuses to be examined, ‎let alone treated--

142
11:43.933 --> 11:46.185
‎So work on him and win him over.

143
11:46.268 --> 11:49.688
‎And if we promise ‎to get support for the victims,

144
11:49.772 --> 11:51.857
‎it'll paint a great picture of justice.

145
11:51.941 --> 11:55.236
‎Now's the time to show ‎the power of the white coat alliance.

146
11:55.319 --> 11:56.153
‎You mean us, sir?

147
11:56.862 --> 11:58.405
‎That med school quota issue?

148
11:59.114 --> 12:01.575
‎We can handle that on our end after this.

149
12:01.659 --> 12:03.536
‎It'd boost public opinion of doctors too.

150
12:03.619 --> 12:04.828
‎Wow, this is just…

151
12:04.912 --> 12:07.498
‎It would be ideal if I could do it myself.

152
12:07.581 --> 12:11.001
‎I'd take out the bullet and show everyone.

153
12:11.085 --> 12:12.253
‎That would be amazing.

154
12:12.336 --> 12:15.214
‎-Why didn't you become a surgeon? ‎-Such a shame.

155
12:15.297 --> 12:16.382
‎Why us?

156
12:17.550 --> 12:19.552
‎Why insist on having the surgery here?

157
12:20.344 --> 12:22.137
‎Because no one else will do it.

158
12:22.221 --> 12:23.806
‎We already asked around.

159
12:23.889 --> 12:25.057
‎We won't do it either.

160
12:25.140 --> 12:27.059
‎Magnolia made the decision.

161
12:27.142 --> 12:30.980
‎You expect us to follow a decision ‎that might jeopardize the hospital?

162
12:33.232 --> 12:35.067
‎The view here is a bit off.

163
12:35.776 --> 12:36.902
‎Director Bu.

164
12:36.986 --> 12:39.947
‎Ever wonder why the director's office ‎is on such an awkward floor?

165
12:46.328 --> 12:47.371
‎Haven't opened it, have you?

166
12:48.163 --> 12:50.624
‎This door connects directly ‎to the parking lot.

167
12:51.834 --> 12:55.296
‎In this position, ‎you can't always use the front door.

168
12:55.379 --> 12:58.465
‎Lower floors undermine your authority, ‎while higher floors make it hard to run.

169
12:58.549 --> 13:02.428
‎But here, it's easy to slip away or bolt ‎if things go sideways.

170
13:03.887 --> 13:06.515
‎Don't assume you'll never use this door.

171
13:10.603 --> 13:13.939
‎We're discussing something important, ‎so come back later.

172
13:14.023 --> 13:15.941
‎I'm sorry, but this is really urgent.

173
13:16.775 --> 13:19.820
‎Sir, a reporter keeps calling.

174
13:24.074 --> 13:26.952
‎They say the foundation is discussing ‎shutting down the hospital

175
13:27.036 --> 13:28.037
‎and want our comments.

176
13:28.746 --> 13:31.206
‎It's said to have leaked ‎from the main hospital

177
13:31.290 --> 13:33.542
‎that we've been struggling ‎with mounting deficits.

178
13:34.126 --> 13:35.002
‎Director Bu.

179
13:35.085 --> 13:38.964
‎The reporter even mentioned ‎the exact deficit amount.

180
13:39.048 --> 13:40.799
‎We need to shut this story down.

181
13:48.932 --> 13:49.808
‎So we're the patsy.

182
13:50.851 --> 13:53.354
‎-What did he just say? ‎-Is he serious?

183
13:53.437 --> 13:55.606
‎What did you say? A patsy for what?

184
13:55.689 --> 13:57.608
‎Tell me I'm wrong.

185
13:59.318 --> 14:01.862
‎Do you think we don't know, Director?

186
14:01.945 --> 14:03.322
‎We know everything.

187
14:03.405 --> 14:05.783
‎Listen, it's unseemly to be so reluctant

188
14:05.866 --> 14:07.993
‎when a patient's life is on the line.

189
14:09.745 --> 14:11.747
‎Dr. Do Yun-sik.

190
14:11.830 --> 14:15.376
‎Don't you think it's ridiculous ‎for you to say that?

191
14:15.459 --> 14:17.378
‎-What did you say? ‎-Sit down.

192
14:17.461 --> 14:19.463
‎Anyone not in neuro has no say.

193
14:19.546 --> 14:20.464
‎Sir, please…

194
14:21.131 --> 14:22.341
‎Please stop.

195
14:22.424 --> 14:24.385
‎Look at you. All right.

196
14:24.468 --> 14:27.304
‎So now you're acting like ‎you're in neuro too, huh?

197
14:27.888 --> 14:29.431
‎Are you learning a lot from Bae?

198
14:30.015 --> 14:31.725
‎You can't even do a craniotomy. ‎Stay out of this.

199
14:31.809 --> 14:32.643
‎What?

200
14:33.185 --> 14:34.728
‎You should watch what you say.

201
14:34.812 --> 14:37.856
‎It's either death on the table ‎or a vegetative state.

202
14:37.940 --> 14:41.193
‎There's no guarantee ‎he'll come out of the OR with no deficits.

203
14:41.276 --> 14:43.654
‎If this isn't unloading ‎a high-risk surgery, what is?

204
14:43.737 --> 14:46.156
‎You haven't even seen any scans yet,

205
14:46.240 --> 14:47.992
‎so why would you say that?

206
14:48.075 --> 14:51.537
‎Everyone under the sun will be watching

207
14:52.246 --> 14:53.872
‎to see how this turns out.

208
14:54.456 --> 14:55.958
‎Why perform this surgery at all?

209
14:56.041 --> 14:57.376
‎Who's going to do it?

210
14:57.459 --> 14:59.378
‎Are you?

211
14:59.920 --> 15:01.296
‎Who?

212
15:03.757 --> 15:05.342
‎I will!

213
15:11.473 --> 15:12.516
‎I'll operate.

214
15:15.477 --> 15:17.604
‎Dr. Gye will operate.

215
15:18.689 --> 15:20.774
‎-What? ‎-They'll take the bait.

216
15:21.442 --> 15:24.778
‎Both Dr. Gye and Ms. Jang ‎won't be able to resist.

217
15:25.738 --> 15:27.072
‎But if she fails…

218
15:27.156 --> 15:29.158
‎We won't be responsible for that outcome.

219
15:29.825 --> 15:32.119
‎It'll be entirely on Dr. Gye and Ms. Jang.

220
15:34.079 --> 15:38.625
‎This could be our chance ‎to kick Dr. Gye out for good.

221
15:39.793 --> 15:41.920
‎Magnolia won't stand back if she fails,

222
15:42.004 --> 15:43.797
‎and public opinion will also…

223
15:45.382 --> 15:47.134
‎We won't be going down alone.

224
15:48.135 --> 15:49.511
‎White coat alliance, right?

225
15:50.512 --> 15:51.638
‎So if we go down,

226
15:52.765 --> 15:53.891
‎we go down together.

227
16:22.586 --> 16:25.923
‎Given we're handling everything ‎from persuasion to surgery,

228
16:26.632 --> 16:28.133
‎this is a bit weak.

229
16:28.634 --> 16:30.886
‎You'll get another one of these ‎when it's done.

230
16:30.969 --> 16:32.262
‎Sounds good.

231
16:34.223 --> 16:35.099
‎You're not taking it?

232
16:36.600 --> 16:37.601
‎I'll take it all at once.

233
16:38.393 --> 16:41.021
‎I went shopping at the department store,

234
16:41.105 --> 16:42.147
‎so I have a lot to carry.

235
16:43.023 --> 16:44.066
‎I'll see you soon.

236
16:53.826 --> 16:55.994
‎She just assumes ‎the surgery will be a success?

237
17:11.426 --> 17:13.512
‎I was in the middle of a grocery run

238
17:14.304 --> 17:16.640
‎when he called out of the blue ‎and told me to come.

239
17:17.349 --> 17:20.477
‎What does he expect me to do ‎after bringing up something like that?

240
17:20.978 --> 17:23.355
‎He basically said we have to do it.

241
17:24.982 --> 17:25.983
‎So I guess we'll oblige.

242
17:27.693 --> 17:31.405
‎I had no idea he'd call again so soon.

243
17:32.197 --> 17:35.409
‎I didn't even ask him the amount ‎because I was trying to play it cool.

244
17:35.951 --> 17:36.910
‎Let's see here.

245
17:37.619 --> 17:40.789
‎Considering the depth of the shopping bag

246
17:41.456 --> 17:43.417
‎and the size of a 50,000-won bill,

247
17:43.500 --> 17:45.335
‎it'd roughly come out to…

248
17:46.920 --> 17:47.880
‎this amount.

249
17:50.924 --> 17:52.092
‎I think we can…

250
17:52.176 --> 17:55.721
‎Don't keep us in suspense ‎and tell us already.

251
17:57.306 --> 17:58.140
‎We can finally…

252
18:00.934 --> 18:01.768
‎get a new car.

253
18:04.271 --> 18:07.232
‎-Nice! ‎-Thank you, God. Thank you, Buddha.

254
18:07.774 --> 18:10.611
‎Every extra day we get to live ‎is thanks to you, Su-jeong.

255
18:11.195 --> 18:13.030
‎Definitely. That car was a death trap.

256
18:13.113 --> 18:14.489
‎I prayed every time I got in it.

257
18:14.573 --> 18:17.534
‎We spend more time pushing it ‎than riding in it these days.

258
18:17.618 --> 18:19.328
‎Let's look up some cars.

259
18:19.411 --> 18:21.121
‎We clean up their messes,

260
18:21.705 --> 18:22.789
‎and he sets a trap?

261
18:25.751 --> 18:27.920
‎He had everyone there to set you up.

262
18:28.962 --> 18:30.797
‎He wanted them to see you step up

263
18:30.881 --> 18:32.549
‎to pin it on you if it goes wrong.

264
18:34.426 --> 18:36.553
‎I texted you knowing he would.

265
18:39.139 --> 18:40.265
‎Not happy to be back in surgery?

266
18:42.935 --> 18:45.270
‎I've been doing appendectomies all week.

267
18:45.354 --> 18:47.689
‎I know. Stop calling me.

268
18:48.315 --> 18:50.776
‎Thanks to you, ‎I've only done appies all week too.

269
18:51.944 --> 18:53.820
‎And since you finish too quickly,

270
18:54.321 --> 18:56.281
‎surgeries keep rolling in, ‎and I get even busier.

271
19:00.953 --> 19:01.787
‎Yes?

272
19:03.247 --> 19:04.081
‎This will help.

273
19:04.164 --> 19:05.332
‎I have some too.

274
19:08.377 --> 19:11.213
‎Can't you just match everyone else's pace?

275
19:11.296 --> 19:14.258
‎Stop doing back-to-back surgeries. ‎I can barely…

276
19:14.341 --> 19:16.260
‎Get to the conference hall right now.

277
19:16.969 --> 19:18.053
‎Tell them you'll do it.

278
19:18.971 --> 19:19.805
‎Do what?

279
19:25.477 --> 19:26.395
‎What--

280
19:28.855 --> 19:31.608
‎Bullet, brain, surgery.

281
19:37.155 --> 19:39.157
‎Have some more. Enjoy.

282
19:39.241 --> 19:40.993
‎-Okay. ‎-This too.

283
19:46.081 --> 19:47.165
‎Over here.

284
19:47.249 --> 19:49.751
‎-Hello, young doctor. ‎-Hello.

285
19:49.835 --> 19:53.880
‎I'm so relieved the hospital ‎assigned you to this case, Dr. Park.

286
19:54.756 --> 19:56.591
‎I haven't been on a train in a while,

287
19:56.675 --> 19:58.593
‎so I'm a bit excited.

288
19:59.386 --> 20:01.305
‎I did all of my assignments too.

289
20:01.388 --> 20:04.725
‎Here are the ones the hospital gave me ‎and the ones I found.

290
20:05.309 --> 20:06.351
‎I read them too.

291
20:06.852 --> 20:07.978
‎Oh, of course you did.

292
20:08.061 --> 20:09.146
‎I just thought…

293
20:09.229 --> 20:10.981
‎She'll read them again on the train.

294
20:11.064 --> 20:12.607
‎-Here, eat this. ‎-Thank you.

295
20:15.277 --> 20:16.820
‎Dr. Jo, over here!

296
20:16.903 --> 20:18.572
‎-Oh, come in. ‎-Here.

297
20:19.448 --> 20:21.366
‎-Join us. ‎-Hello.

298
20:21.450 --> 20:23.452
‎Don't feel awkward.

299
20:23.535 --> 20:24.995
‎We already know each other.

300
20:25.662 --> 20:27.622
‎-Come here. ‎-Okay.

301
20:27.706 --> 20:30.334
‎I came because you asked, ‎but you didn't have to include me.

302
20:30.417 --> 20:33.962
‎We didn't get to have dinner last time ‎because of that damn bastard.

303
20:34.046 --> 20:35.839
‎I was so disappointed.

304
20:35.922 --> 20:38.467
‎But since you agreed to do it,

305
20:38.550 --> 20:40.635
‎we might as well go together.

306
20:40.719 --> 20:42.512
‎But why bring an anesthesiologist?

307
20:42.596 --> 20:45.599
‎Just look at the cheerful goof

308
20:46.475 --> 20:47.601
‎and the moody glutton.

309
20:48.185 --> 20:49.561
‎Would you let them operate on you?

310
20:49.644 --> 20:52.856
‎We need at least one person ‎who looks like a doctor, right?

311
20:53.440 --> 20:54.858
‎So just come along, okay?

312
21:03.617 --> 21:05.160
‎-Here, have this. ‎-Okay.

313
21:06.995 --> 21:08.705
‎Looks like this place is done for the day.

314
21:09.831 --> 21:11.041
‎So is my wallet.

315
21:12.292 --> 21:13.794
‎I'll let you off the hook for today.

316
21:14.878 --> 21:17.255
‎You seem to know Dr. Gye pretty well.

317
21:17.339 --> 21:20.008
‎-You two must be friends now, right? ‎-I wouldn't say that.

318
21:21.718 --> 21:23.678
‎Oh, right.

319
21:23.762 --> 21:25.722
‎It's a long trip,

320
21:25.806 --> 21:29.017
‎so let's recharge our batteries ‎before we go.

321
21:29.518 --> 21:30.435
‎Okay, okay.

322
21:31.186 --> 21:33.438
‎-Here, have one. ‎-Thank you.

323
21:39.152 --> 21:40.320
‎This is good.

324
21:49.287 --> 21:50.288
‎I'm full of energy now.

325
21:51.540 --> 21:55.419
‎Are you two reading the same text I am?

326
21:55.502 --> 21:58.505
‎On the train yet? Snacking now? ‎What about presents? Gwangju specialties?

327
21:58.588 --> 22:00.340
‎Thinking of me? At the train station yet?

328
22:00.424 --> 22:02.551
‎No gift, you're a buzzkill. ‎Get me one, you're a baller.

329
22:02.634 --> 22:04.094
‎-Get it, or triggered? ‎-Oh, Dr. Kim?

330
22:04.177 --> 22:06.096
‎Talk to me, delicate Lady Macbeth. ‎No? I'm sad. Boo.

331
22:06.179 --> 22:07.973
‎My phone's turned into a pager.

332
22:08.640 --> 22:09.474
‎I'll handle this.

333
22:11.059 --> 22:12.894
‎The ER must be quiet right now.

334
22:14.312 --> 22:15.230
‎You're cruel.

335
22:15.313 --> 22:18.024
‎I agree. That's really harsh.

336
22:20.819 --> 22:22.863
‎Jeez. He really must have no friends.

337
22:25.657 --> 22:26.658
‎What is it?

338
22:28.660 --> 22:29.703
‎That's mine.

339
22:32.122 --> 22:33.748
‎I have lots of friends.

340
22:33.832 --> 22:35.083
‎I'm totally popular.

341
22:37.335 --> 22:38.170
‎Unlike him.

342
22:38.253 --> 22:40.130
‎What? I have tons of friends.

343
22:40.213 --> 22:42.048
‎-No, you don't. ‎-I really do.

344
22:42.132 --> 22:44.009
‎-How many? ‎-Well, I…

345
22:44.092 --> 22:46.553
‎Three, two, one. See? Zero friends.

346
22:59.816 --> 23:03.111
‎I used to run a small shoe store.

347
23:04.905 --> 23:09.201
‎Children's Day, Parents' Day, ‎and Teacher's Day were all in May,

348
23:09.826 --> 23:11.953
‎so it was an exciting month ‎for shopkeepers like me.

349
23:12.871 --> 23:13.914
‎But then…

350
23:28.053 --> 23:29.554
‎GWANGJU, 1980

351
23:29.638 --> 23:30.555
‎-Have a good day. ‎-Thanks!

352
23:30.639 --> 23:33.850
‎Look, I'll show you these shoes here

353
23:33.934 --> 23:35.977
‎if you show me some money.

354
23:36.478 --> 23:37.604
‎Do you have any right now?

355
23:38.313 --> 23:39.648
‎Show me the shoes first.

356
23:39.731 --> 23:41.816
‎Gosh, you little punk.

357
23:42.984 --> 23:46.738
‎Your older brother is Seung-beom, right? ‎The shoe shiner by the provincial office?

358
23:46.821 --> 23:48.406
‎How did you know that?

359
23:49.407 --> 23:51.576
‎I guess us tiger brothers ‎are pretty famous.

360
23:52.577 --> 23:53.787
‎Look at you.

361
23:54.829 --> 23:58.250
‎You're as big as a cat. Tiger, my foot.

362
23:58.333 --> 24:00.126
‎Goodness, that's hilarious.

363
24:01.211 --> 24:05.298
‎So, you've been pacing around my shop ‎these past few days.

364
24:05.382 --> 24:06.716
‎Was it to see some shoes?

365
24:07.425 --> 24:08.843
‎You little rascal.

366
24:08.927 --> 24:11.096
‎Your older brother shines shoes all day

367
24:11.179 --> 24:14.015
‎to support you and your mother.

368
24:14.099 --> 24:18.019
‎And you go around spending his money ‎on buying shoes?

369
24:18.103 --> 24:19.020
‎It's my money.

370
24:19.104 --> 24:20.063
‎Is it?

371
24:21.273 --> 24:23.275
‎I'm sorry, kid.

372
24:23.358 --> 24:26.611
‎I saved all my money ‎to buy my brother a pair of shoes.

373
24:29.155 --> 24:30.490
‎Goodness.

374
24:32.784 --> 24:34.577
‎You resemble him.

375
24:35.161 --> 24:38.373
‎You're sharp, just like your brother.

376
24:40.125 --> 24:40.959
‎Really?

377
24:41.876 --> 24:44.629
‎But we're not even related by blood.

378
24:46.089 --> 24:47.382
‎When I was four,

379
24:47.465 --> 24:51.136
‎my birth mom rented a room ‎in my mom's place.

380
24:51.219 --> 24:53.179
‎But my birth mom ‎left me there and took off.

381
24:54.097 --> 24:56.766
‎That's how my mom and brother ‎became my family.

382
24:57.559 --> 24:58.852
‎If it weren't for me,

383
24:59.602 --> 25:01.479
‎he wouldn't have to shine shoes so much.

384
25:02.230 --> 25:04.190
‎He could maybe work every other day.

385
25:04.816 --> 25:06.735
‎Don't be silly. You're his little brother.

386
25:08.695 --> 25:09.529
‎Wait here.

387
25:12.115 --> 25:15.952
‎My brother likes classical music.

388
25:16.536 --> 25:18.371
‎And my brother is… What's it called?

389
25:19.789 --> 25:20.957
‎He's intelligible.

390
25:21.958 --> 25:23.752
‎You mean "intelligent"!

391
25:23.835 --> 25:27.505
‎Intelligible means ‎being understood and such.

392
25:28.381 --> 25:30.925
‎Anyway, you know what I mean, right?

393
25:31.634 --> 25:33.470
‎I'm saying he's really smart.

394
25:34.512 --> 25:37.891
‎He wants to learn the piano. ‎It won't take a guy like him long.

395
25:40.477 --> 25:43.104
‎HANBAEK DRESS SHOES

396
25:43.188 --> 25:44.898
‎Let's see here.

397
25:46.107 --> 25:47.442
‎Here it is.

398
25:48.193 --> 25:49.110
‎Take a look.

399
25:49.903 --> 25:50.987
‎Will this do?

400
25:56.034 --> 25:57.118
‎Yes, it will.

401
26:36.116 --> 26:36.950
‎Here.

402
26:38.159 --> 26:39.077
‎Take it.

403
26:39.744 --> 26:40.578
‎Huh?

404
26:41.538 --> 26:42.414
‎What about the money?

405
26:44.499 --> 26:46.167
‎So, about these shoes.

406
26:47.335 --> 26:50.713
‎Take a good look at the laces.

407
26:51.756 --> 26:53.383
‎If you look carefully,

408
26:53.466 --> 26:56.428
‎the laces are slightly uneven.

409
26:57.804 --> 26:59.514
‎-Are they? ‎-Come on.

410
27:00.348 --> 27:03.852
‎You seem pretty smart, ‎but your eyesight must be bad.

411
27:06.855 --> 27:08.523
‎I can't sell them, so just take them.

412
27:10.608 --> 27:14.195
‎Save your money

413
27:15.738 --> 27:17.824
‎so you can buy your brother a piano.

414
27:24.831 --> 27:27.500
‎Hey, what are you doing?

415
27:27.584 --> 27:28.918
‎"I won't forget your kindness."

416
27:29.002 --> 27:31.004
‎My mom taught me to bow when saying that.

417
27:31.087 --> 27:34.549
‎Goodness, I thought for a second ‎that I had to give you pocket money.

418
27:36.092 --> 27:38.970
‎Wait right here. ‎I'll get you some shoe polish.

419
27:46.060 --> 27:47.520
‎-They've got guns! ‎-What?

420
27:47.604 --> 27:49.439
‎-He threw something! ‎-What's happening?

421
27:53.568 --> 27:54.611
‎Is there another protest?

422
27:56.237 --> 27:59.324
‎Gosh, are people running ‎from the provincial office?

423
28:01.201 --> 28:02.869
‎Don't go there! Come over here!

424
28:04.120 --> 28:05.914
‎Wait, my brother!

425
28:09.042 --> 28:09.876
‎No, don't go.

426
28:09.959 --> 28:10.960
‎I have to go to my brother.

427
28:11.044 --> 28:12.253
‎No, you can't!

428
28:12.337 --> 28:13.630
‎If something happens to him…

429
28:15.173 --> 28:17.008
‎Let go. I said let go of me!

430
28:29.729 --> 28:30.772
‎Run!

431
28:31.606 --> 28:32.440
‎Hurry!

432
28:34.108 --> 28:34.984
‎No.

433
28:37.487 --> 28:38.363
‎No.

434
29:02.345 --> 29:03.346
‎Seung-beom!

435
29:11.229 --> 29:12.188
‎Seung-beom!

436
29:24.492 --> 29:27.412
‎We just listened to Michel Polnier's ‎"Qui a tué grand' maman."

437
29:27.495 --> 29:28.329
‎Su-jeong.

438
29:29.414 --> 29:33.626
‎This song is well known in Gwangju ‎as the original version of "Song of May."

439
29:34.752 --> 29:37.505
‎Back when "Song of May" was banned,

440
29:37.589 --> 29:40.925
‎stations nationwide would play this ‎around May 18th in tribute.

441
29:41.009 --> 29:42.135
‎We get off at the next stop.

442
29:44.971 --> 29:48.975
‎It's good to know ‎someone has been looking after him.

443
29:49.058 --> 29:52.228
‎They were patients in the same hospital, ‎but he's a doctor now.

444
29:53.521 --> 29:55.940
‎He really goes there every day?

445
29:58.902 --> 30:01.321
‎They couldn't find his brother's body.

446
30:02.488 --> 30:04.324
‎So he hasn't been laid to rest yet.

447
30:06.242 --> 30:08.703
‎They say many are still unaccounted for.

448
30:09.913 --> 30:11.456
‎That's why he goes there.

449
30:15.293 --> 30:16.920
‎He shines shoes for a living

450
30:17.545 --> 30:21.549
‎and goes there straight after work, ‎come rain or shine.

451
30:22.300 --> 30:24.302
‎For more than 40 years, ‎pretty much his whole life.

452
30:29.098 --> 30:30.934
‎He stopped talking at some point.

453
30:31.517 --> 30:33.269
‎He just refuses.

454
30:34.854 --> 30:36.773
‎The last thing he said was,

455
30:36.856 --> 30:38.900
‎"It's all my fault."

456
30:39.817 --> 30:41.861
‎"I want to die because I'm alive."

457
30:42.445 --> 30:44.364
‎"But dying is too easy,

458
30:45.031 --> 30:47.617
‎so I'll pay the price by living in pain."

459
31:23.361 --> 31:25.321
‎WOO JAE-GYEONG INTERNAL MEDICINE

460
31:45.133 --> 31:46.134
‎Hello.

461
31:47.760 --> 31:49.512
‎I'm sorry for keeping you waiting.

462
31:49.595 --> 31:50.596
‎Please come in.

463
31:55.643 --> 31:58.396
‎These two were ‎also in the hospital with us.

464
31:58.479 --> 31:59.981
‎They want to talk to him too.

465
32:02.108 --> 32:02.942
‎Please take a seat.

466
32:15.830 --> 32:18.499
‎Are you saying she performed this surgery

467
32:18.583 --> 32:21.002
‎and will be doing Sang-beom's as well?

468
32:21.085 --> 32:22.086
‎Yes, that's right.

469
32:22.962 --> 32:25.798
‎Everyone here is an excellent doctor.

470
32:27.675 --> 32:28.801
‎I see.

471
32:29.677 --> 32:30.511
‎Amazing.

472
32:31.429 --> 32:32.889
‎I've never seen anything like it.

473
32:37.935 --> 32:40.063
‎Why aren't you saying anything?

474
32:40.813 --> 32:43.608
‎The government is paying for your surgery.

475
32:43.691 --> 32:45.109
‎Lower your voice.

476
32:45.193 --> 32:47.487
‎We can hear you just fine.

477
32:48.446 --> 32:51.699
‎Do you want to wither away ‎like Geun-sik did a while back?

478
32:52.325 --> 32:54.243
‎Why would you bring that up?

479
32:54.911 --> 32:58.539
‎How much longer ‎do we need to see that happen?

480
32:59.582 --> 33:01.834
‎If we keep disappearing one by one,

481
33:02.585 --> 33:04.253
‎everyone will forget what happened.

482
33:04.754 --> 33:07.048
‎It'll be wiped clean ‎like it never happened at all.

483
33:07.131 --> 33:08.800
‎Stop it already.

484
33:09.884 --> 33:10.968
‎Sang-beom.

485
33:11.052 --> 33:13.221
‎Do whatever you want.

486
33:13.304 --> 33:15.765
‎We shouldn't have come. ‎Let's go, Yeong-pyo.

487
33:15.848 --> 33:18.601
‎Do you know what's really terrifying?

488
33:19.435 --> 33:21.896
‎Being wiped clean ‎wouldn't actually be the worst of it.

489
33:21.979 --> 33:24.690
‎They'll say North Korea was behind it,

490
33:24.774 --> 33:27.360
‎that we killed each other in a firefight,

491
33:27.443 --> 33:30.446
‎and that we opened fire ‎on the military first!

492
33:31.364 --> 33:34.158
‎That's what they'll write ‎after wiping our stories clean.

493
33:34.992 --> 33:36.911
‎If we keep disappearing one by one,

494
33:37.662 --> 33:38.996
‎that's what will happen!

495
33:41.249 --> 33:42.416
‎We need to live long.

496
33:43.459 --> 33:45.753
‎We need to live long, just to spite them.

497
33:46.796 --> 33:48.798
‎Come on, Sang-beom.

498
33:50.550 --> 33:52.510
‎Say something!

499
33:54.679 --> 33:57.014
‎There you are, Ms. Jin.

500
33:57.515 --> 33:59.809
‎Please pass that around.

501
34:00.768 --> 34:01.978
‎Good.

502
34:02.061 --> 34:04.730
‎Go outside and blow off some steam.

503
34:06.524 --> 34:09.193
‎Sang-beom, you know how he feels.

504
34:09.277 --> 34:10.111
‎Right?

505
34:10.820 --> 34:12.864
‎Every time Yeong-pyo drinks, ‎he goes on about

506
34:12.947 --> 34:15.324
‎how heartbreaking it is ‎that you've had to live that way

507
34:15.867 --> 34:17.368
‎all these years.

508
34:17.451 --> 34:20.413
‎He thinks about ‎how lonely it must've been for you,

509
34:21.205 --> 34:22.874
‎and he cries every time.

510
34:25.626 --> 34:26.836
‎Isn't it funny?

511
34:27.795 --> 34:30.006
‎He's almost 60, you know.

512
34:31.632 --> 34:33.259
‎But in our eyes,

513
34:33.885 --> 34:35.344
‎you'll always be

514
34:36.012 --> 34:38.389
‎the same little 12-year-old kid

515
34:39.015 --> 34:41.184
‎who cried and begged to go home.

516
34:42.602 --> 34:45.521
‎Asleep or awake, ‎you'd ask for your brother.

517
34:46.522 --> 34:49.108
‎And asleep or awake, ‎you'd ask for your mom.

518
34:50.026 --> 34:51.360
‎Do you remember?

519
34:51.986 --> 34:55.364
‎You'd wake up in the middle of the night ‎crying and sobbing,

520
34:55.448 --> 34:58.075
‎"It's too heavy."

521
34:58.159 --> 35:00.453
‎You kept repeating that over and over.

522
35:00.953 --> 35:03.664
‎Gosh, it made me wonder ‎how frightened you must've been

523
35:04.332 --> 35:08.002
‎to mix up "It's too scary" ‎with "It's too heavy."

524
35:08.836 --> 35:10.463
‎It broke my heart.

525
35:18.638 --> 35:19.722
‎Being a doctor myself,

526
35:21.182 --> 35:23.267
‎I have an idea of how risky it is.

527
35:23.851 --> 35:26.646
‎There's a high chance ‎the surgery will fail, right?

528
35:34.737 --> 35:35.863
‎Will he be able to

529
35:37.240 --> 35:38.366
‎come back?

530
35:40.159 --> 35:41.160
‎I might fail.

531
35:43.663 --> 35:45.164
‎If I fail, you'll die.

532
35:47.583 --> 35:48.918
‎You don't have to do the surgery.

533
35:49.835 --> 35:50.962
‎You might be uncomfortable,

534
35:51.921 --> 35:53.422
‎but you're still alive.

535
35:55.466 --> 35:58.803
‎She's saying she respects ‎Mr. Oh's wishes and opinion.

536
35:58.886 --> 36:00.346
‎But will you be okay with it?

537
36:01.722 --> 36:02.974
‎Just existing like this?

538
36:08.396 --> 36:12.733
‎You've spent all these years ‎simply existing in pain.

539
36:14.443 --> 36:15.861
‎Are you really okay with it?

540
36:24.996 --> 36:26.414
‎This thick file only contains

541
36:27.748 --> 36:29.208
‎painkiller prescriptions.

542
36:38.676 --> 36:40.678
‎Dying… I mean, the end

543
36:41.929 --> 36:42.930
‎is the same either way.

544
36:45.349 --> 36:49.437
‎But if we do nothing, ‎there's no chance at all.

545
36:58.738 --> 37:01.198
‎Like Dr. Gye said,

546
37:02.616 --> 37:04.118
‎you don't have to do the surgery.

547
37:04.618 --> 37:06.620
‎But at least let us examine you.

548
37:06.704 --> 37:09.540
‎We need the exam results to know for sure.

549
37:10.041 --> 37:11.584
‎After you see the results,

550
37:12.084 --> 37:13.544
‎you're free to leave without surgery.

551
37:14.211 --> 37:15.963
‎Just take a few scans, okay?

552
37:49.288 --> 37:50.247
‎Goodness.

553
37:51.082 --> 37:52.750
‎Why just the scans?

554
37:52.833 --> 37:54.502
‎While you're in Seoul,

555
37:55.086 --> 37:57.088
‎look around and eat some good food too.

556
37:58.589 --> 37:59.548
‎Sang-beom.

557
38:00.383 --> 38:02.843
‎It's time you lived a little.

558
38:27.076 --> 38:27.993
‎Well…

559
38:29.495 --> 38:33.249
‎I guess everyone felt sad ‎to see Sang-beom off.

560
38:34.208 --> 38:35.960
‎So I came on behalf of the others.

561
38:36.043 --> 38:39.213
‎Once we arrive, he'll be admitted, ‎and we'll run some scans.

562
38:39.880 --> 38:40.881
‎We'll keep you updated.

563
38:43.968 --> 38:46.429
‎Please call me whenever you feel worried.

564
38:46.512 --> 38:47.555
‎I'll answer every time.

565
38:48.139 --> 38:49.014
‎Oh, right.

566
38:49.515 --> 38:50.891
‎Here's some ‎gimbap‎.

567
38:59.483 --> 39:01.735
‎I'll be there on the day of your surgery.

568
39:02.319 --> 39:03.154
‎See you then, okay?

569
39:04.864 --> 39:06.323
‎This is really good.

570
39:07.241 --> 39:08.367
‎My word.

571
39:08.993 --> 39:11.328
‎She's got skills to match her appetite.

572
39:11.412 --> 39:12.371
‎Don't worry.

573
39:12.913 --> 39:16.417
‎I should've made ‎ten or a hundred more then.

574
39:22.089 --> 39:25.092
‎Everyone chipped in a little.

575
39:25.676 --> 39:27.136
‎Come on, take it.

576
39:27.219 --> 39:28.429
‎Just take it.

577
39:32.099 --> 39:32.975
‎There we go.

578
39:33.934 --> 39:36.103
‎Everyone has it hard.

579
39:36.187 --> 39:39.356
‎But when it comes to ‎how much we care about you,

580
39:39.440 --> 39:42.610
‎we're just as wealthy as ‎Lee Byeong-chull or Elon Musk.

581
39:42.693 --> 39:44.778
‎I know the government is covering

582
39:44.862 --> 39:46.238
‎-all your medical bills, ‎-Stop eating.

583
39:46.322 --> 39:49.825
‎but a thick wallet ‎keeps you standing tall.

584
39:50.784 --> 39:53.621
‎Hold your head high when you get there.

585
39:54.288 --> 39:58.250
‎Because we did nothing wrong.

586
40:17.394 --> 40:19.605
‎Hey, what are you…

587
41:06.068 --> 41:07.778
‎Attention, passengers.

588
41:08.612 --> 41:12.324
‎Please be careful ‎while the train is moving.

589
41:16.829 --> 41:19.790
‎Thank you for riding with us today.

590
41:20.791 --> 41:23.419
‎We hope you have a pleasant journey.

591
41:40.144 --> 41:41.604
‎He'll come back.

592
41:45.357 --> 41:47.318
‎Why did he get on his knees and bow?

593
41:51.697 --> 41:54.491
‎Why did he have to ‎get on his knees and bow?

594
41:58.579 --> 41:59.955
‎He'll be fine.

595
42:02.374 --> 42:03.250
‎I know he will.

596
42:24.104 --> 42:27.983
‎Thanks to you, we got to ride a train, ‎take a nice long trip,

597
42:28.067 --> 42:30.402
‎and receive all this delicious food.

598
42:32.488 --> 42:34.365
‎Has it been a while ‎since you took a train?

599
42:39.495 --> 42:40.788
‎Is this your first time on a train?

600
42:44.458 --> 42:46.418
‎Oh, I see.

601
42:47.044 --> 42:51.924
‎So you've never been anywhere ‎other than Gwangju?

602
42:55.719 --> 42:56.887
‎Why?

603
43:13.362 --> 43:16.490
‎BECAUSE I FEEL GUILTY

604
43:27.292 --> 43:30.212
‎GUSEO UNIVERSITY SEONAM MEDICAL CENTER

605
43:33.215 --> 43:38.929
‎2. PRESENT ILLNESS: INJURY FROM ‎BULLET FRAGMENT IN OCCIPITAL REGION

606
43:45.269 --> 43:46.145
‎What on earth…

607
43:48.439 --> 43:50.107
‎happened that day?

608
44:01.243 --> 44:02.077
‎Please have this.

609
44:03.245 --> 44:04.830
‎Did you enjoy your meal today?

610
44:10.335 --> 44:13.464
‎Mr. Oh, did you sleep comfortably?

611
44:15.466 --> 44:16.300
‎That's a relief.

612
44:17.217 --> 44:19.344
‎The weather is so nice today.

613
44:19.428 --> 44:22.598
‎-It really is, isn't it? ‎-It's already spring.

614
44:23.182 --> 44:25.225
‎The walking path here is lovely. ‎You should check it out.

615
44:25.309 --> 44:26.393
‎Why don't I take you?

616
44:47.456 --> 44:48.624
‎You need to rest comfortably.

617
44:49.374 --> 44:51.960
‎The hospital provided this room for you,

618
44:53.253 --> 44:54.713
‎so please don't worry.

619
44:56.757 --> 44:58.800
‎Gosh, thank you all for your hard work!

620
44:58.884 --> 45:01.970
‎-Hello. ‎-Goodness, Mr. Oh.

621
45:02.054 --> 45:03.972
‎It's very nice to meet you.

622
45:04.056 --> 45:06.642
‎I'm Kim Chang-su, ‎president of the Medical Association.

623
45:06.725 --> 45:07.976
‎I'm Mayor Im Ho-seok.

624
45:08.644 --> 45:10.687
‎Are you settling in okay?

625
45:11.271 --> 45:15.150
‎I hope you make yourself comfortable, ‎have a smooth surgery,

626
45:15.234 --> 45:19.530
‎and heal from your emotional wounds ‎before you leave.

627
45:19.613 --> 45:20.697
‎Now then.

628
45:20.781 --> 45:23.992
‎-You have such a kind face. ‎-Come on…

629
45:25.077 --> 45:25.911
‎What?

630
45:26.828 --> 45:29.122
‎What do you think you're doing?

631
45:29.206 --> 45:30.958
‎-Gye Su-jeong. ‎-If you're done shaking hands, leave.

632
45:31.542 --> 45:32.376
‎He's my patient.

633
45:33.126 --> 45:35.337
‎-What? ‎-Do you know who this is?

634
45:35.921 --> 45:37.673
‎Dr. Gye, did you just lose your mind?

635
45:38.382 --> 45:40.133
‎Not just now, no.

636
45:40.217 --> 45:41.593
‎I've always been this way.

637
45:41.677 --> 45:42.844
‎You must be Gye Su-jeong.

638
45:43.845 --> 45:45.222
‎-Yeah. ‎-"Yeah"?

639
45:46.348 --> 45:48.809
‎Stop exhausting my patient ‎with boring self-introductions,

640
45:48.892 --> 45:52.688
‎self-praise, long-winded speeches, ‎and a grab for credit.

641
45:53.480 --> 45:55.023
‎Get lost already.

642
45:56.567 --> 45:57.818
‎-"Get lost"? ‎-"Get lost"?

643
45:57.901 --> 45:59.069
‎Dr. Gye!

644
46:00.028 --> 46:01.613
‎Wait, is that a fire alarm?

645
46:02.322 --> 46:03.657
‎What? Is there a fire?

646
46:03.740 --> 46:05.033
‎Is there really a fire?

647
46:05.117 --> 46:06.368
‎-What's going on? ‎-A fire?

648
46:06.451 --> 46:07.828
‎-Sir, we should go. ‎-Follow us.

649
46:07.911 --> 46:09.371
‎-Is there a fire? ‎-Let's go.

650
46:27.806 --> 46:28.640
‎Dr. Gye.

651
46:29.558 --> 46:31.476
‎I suppose from your perspective,

652
46:31.977 --> 46:33.895
‎this is all just a waste of time,

653
46:34.605 --> 46:38.025
‎and we're a bunch of pathetic idiots.

654
46:39.735 --> 46:41.111
‎But you know what?

655
46:41.695 --> 46:45.532
‎The world is shaped and run ‎by people who say "yes,"

656
46:46.366 --> 46:49.286
‎not the ones who say "no."

657
46:51.288 --> 46:53.206
‎Director, we should get out.

658
47:03.091 --> 47:04.009
‎We're fine.

659
47:09.348 --> 47:11.058
‎Dr. Jo, don't tell me you…

660
47:11.141 --> 47:12.934
‎I've always wanted to push that button.

661
47:13.685 --> 47:14.978
‎It practically begs you to push it.

662
47:15.062 --> 47:16.313
‎But who knew I'd do it today?

663
47:17.230 --> 47:19.107
‎I reviewed your scans.

664
47:20.609 --> 47:21.610
‎Mr. Oh.

665
47:23.403 --> 47:24.738
‎Do you see your brother?

666
47:30.535 --> 47:31.662
‎The first time I saw you,

667
47:32.204 --> 47:34.456
‎you were sitting at the end of the bench

668
47:34.539 --> 47:36.166
‎even though it was rather small.

669
47:36.833 --> 47:39.378
‎And you were looking to the side.

670
47:40.837 --> 47:42.589
‎As if someone was sitting next to you.

671
47:43.090 --> 47:45.842
‎He was just looking at the old cemetery…

672
47:52.891 --> 47:54.518
‎You weren't looking into the distance.

673
47:56.436 --> 47:59.815
‎I hear you always wear a notepad ‎and pencil around your neck.

674
48:00.357 --> 48:02.401
‎But not then.

675
48:03.902 --> 48:05.696
‎Because you don't need them ‎to talk to him.

676
48:09.574 --> 48:10.784
‎It was the same

677
48:12.411 --> 48:13.370
‎on the hospital bench.

678
48:15.163 --> 48:16.081
‎After the surgery,

679
48:16.665 --> 48:20.961
‎your seizures, tremors, pain, ‎and other symptoms will lessen.

680
48:21.044 --> 48:24.715
‎The visual and auditory hallucinations ‎will also decrease.

681
48:25.632 --> 48:27.676
‎And so will the chances ‎of seeing your brother.

682
48:31.221 --> 48:33.515
‎I thought you should be aware of this.

683
48:52.534 --> 48:56.621
‎MY BROTHER IS A SYMPTOM?

684
48:57.622 --> 48:58.665
‎Yes.

685
49:07.758 --> 49:11.052
‎NOT A FIGMENT OF MY IMAGINATION?

686
49:13.054 --> 49:13.889
‎You know the answer.

687
49:16.808 --> 49:17.851
‎Dr. Gye.

688
49:19.394 --> 49:20.395
‎The surgery…

689
49:20.979 --> 49:21.938
‎Can you pull it off?

690
49:24.357 --> 49:25.400
‎Yes.

691
49:28.445 --> 49:29.821
‎I don't fail.

692
49:54.679 --> 49:57.933
‎I'M NOT DOING IT

693
50:34.344 --> 50:35.762
‎I wish…

694
50:37.305 --> 50:38.431
‎I could see him too.

695
51:21.057 --> 51:22.976
‎I'M NOT DOING IT

696
51:34.905 --> 51:37.032
‎-What are you doing? ‎-Oh jeez.

697
51:38.199 --> 51:39.409
‎Dr. Jo, you're like a cat.

698
51:39.492 --> 51:42.203
‎-How are you so quiet? ‎-He's probably asleep. Why are you here?

699
51:43.496 --> 51:44.331
‎Right.

700
51:46.374 --> 51:47.542
‎Why are ‎you‎ here?

701
51:47.626 --> 51:50.545
‎Oh, I was on my way home.

702
51:51.880 --> 51:54.507
‎You leave through the third floor ‎and not the first?

703
51:55.800 --> 51:57.886
‎You're smart sometimes.

704
51:59.930 --> 52:01.056
‎Oh, right…

705
52:18.823 --> 52:20.367
‎Oh, this is hot.

706
52:20.450 --> 52:21.952
‎That smells incredible.

707
52:23.912 --> 52:25.121
‎-Hey. ‎-I'm home.

708
52:25.205 --> 52:27.290
‎-Hi there. ‎-Come sit down.

709
52:27.874 --> 52:29.125
‎We need to fry some sausage.

710
52:29.209 --> 52:31.920
‎On top of marinated crab and everything?

711
52:32.003 --> 52:33.797
‎Su-jeong likes it.

712
52:33.880 --> 52:36.383
‎We're having a banquet tonight.

713
52:36.466 --> 52:37.550
‎Wash your hands and sit down.

714
52:39.260 --> 52:40.387
‎Mr. Oh?

715
52:42.305 --> 52:43.181
‎Mr. Oh?

716
52:56.695 --> 52:57.529
‎Damn it.

717
52:58.238 --> 53:00.407
‎-What are you staring at? ‎-Around 7:50 p.m. today,

718
53:00.490 --> 53:03.368
‎Mr. Ji Du-seok, who served ‎as the 11th and 12th president,

719
53:03.451 --> 53:06.413
‎was found collapsed ‎in a golf clubhouse sauna

720
53:06.496 --> 53:07.914
‎in Gyeonggi Province.

721
53:07.998 --> 53:12.210
‎He was found in cardiac arrest ‎and immediately given CPR.

722
53:12.293 --> 53:14.504
‎He is currently being airlifted ‎to the nearest hospital,

723
53:14.587 --> 53:17.090
‎which is the Gyeonggi branch of GUMC.

724
53:17.799 --> 53:20.343
‎The exact cause of his collapse ‎is still unclear…

725
53:20.427 --> 53:21.302
‎PARK TAE-GYEONG

726
53:21.970 --> 53:24.180
‎Dr. Gye, Mr. Oh disappeared.

727
53:24.264 --> 53:27.767
‎We've been looking for a while, ‎but we can't find him.

728
53:33.440 --> 53:35.650
‎Reports say he was still unconscious

729
53:35.734 --> 53:38.486
‎and receiving oxygen support.

730
53:38.570 --> 53:41.823
‎Here is a quick recap ‎of what has happened.

731
53:41.906 --> 53:44.034
‎At around 7:50 p.m.,

732
53:44.117 --> 53:46.661
‎former President Ji Du-seok

733
53:46.745 --> 53:48.955
‎was found unconscious ‎in a golf clubhouse sauna

734
53:49.039 --> 53:51.249
‎located in Gyeonggi Province.

735
54:02.218 --> 54:03.762
‎Dr. Jo, look.

736
54:04.596 --> 54:06.681
‎But where is that?

737
54:07.807 --> 54:08.641
‎The rooftop!

738
54:12.937 --> 54:14.314
‎Dr. Gye, he's on the rooftop.

739
54:57.941 --> 54:59.317
‎There's too much traffic.

740
55:04.697 --> 55:05.740
‎What's that?

741
55:18.002 --> 55:18.837
‎Su-jeong.

742
55:19.462 --> 55:20.630
‎Su-jeong, run!

743
55:21.131 --> 55:22.799
‎You need to stop him!

744
55:22.882 --> 55:23.758
‎No matter what!

745
56:22.609 --> 56:24.110
‎-Dr. Kim? ‎-Hurry up. We're busy.

746
56:24.194 --> 56:25.153
‎EMS helicopter?

747
56:25.236 --> 56:27.030
‎Ji Du-seok is being airlifted in.

748
57:08.238 --> 57:09.739
‎-No! ‎-Mr. Oh!

749
57:21.000 --> 57:22.877
‎No! Grab him!

750
57:24.963 --> 57:26.589
‎-Oh god! ‎-Please pull yourself together.

751
58:21.477 --> 58:23.187
‎Mr. Oh, please!

752
58:39.245 --> 58:40.538
‎Please, Mr. Oh!

753
58:44.417 --> 58:45.877
‎Please…

754
58:47.211 --> 58:48.171
‎Please!

755
58:54.093 --> 58:56.888
‎BECAUSE I FEEL GUILTY

756
59:02.101 --> 59:04.312
‎Please help us.

757
59:16.491 --> 59:17.325
‎Please…

758
59:18.034 --> 59:18.951
‎Please…

759
59:19.661 --> 59:20.495
‎Please…

760
59:21.746 --> 59:22.705
‎Please.

761
59:36.052 --> 59:38.930
‎GUSEO UNIVERSITY SEONAM MEDICAL CENTER

762
59:39.013 --> 59:41.766
‎DOCTOR X: MAFIA IN WHITE

763
01:00:21.723 --> 01:00:23.808
‎DOCTOR X: MAFIA IN WHITE

764
01:00:23.891 --> 01:00:25.852
‎Please calm down. Push a sedative now!

765
01:00:25.935 --> 01:00:28.187
‎They talked about transferring him ‎in the meeting.

766
01:00:28.271 --> 01:00:30.523
‎Does that mean the hospital is giving up?

767
01:00:30.606 --> 01:00:32.108
‎He wants us to discharge him.

768
01:00:32.191 --> 01:00:33.526
‎You have to live!

769
01:00:33.609 --> 01:00:35.486
‎You have to try and live!

770
01:00:35.570 --> 01:00:37.780
‎Mr. Oh Sang-beom has disappeared?

771
01:00:37.864 --> 01:00:38.906
‎Get in!

772
01:00:39.407 --> 01:00:40.742
‎But you know, don't you?

773
01:00:40.825 --> 01:00:42.368
‎There's a way, right?

774
01:00:42.452 --> 01:00:43.369
‎Think.

775
01:00:43.453 --> 01:00:45.121
‎You must think and find a way.

776
01:00:45.204 --> 01:00:48.708
‎Everyone will soon find out ‎about your lie, Dr. Gye.

777
01:00:50.418 --> 01:00:55.423
‎Subtitle translation by: Jenny Kim
